{
 "note": "Read by tools/render_map_thumbnails.py, which draws the pictures, and by tools/export_map_paths.py, which passes each one to the map page. The small picture shown for each actuator. \"records\" is keyed by record id. Each entry holds \"kind\", \"image\" (the picture's path under site/) and either \"sources\" or \"basis\". Kind \"mesh\" is real geometry: the rest shape drawn from the mesh the simulation ran on, with every file used listed in \"sources\" and pinned by repository, commit, path and sha256 (\"draws\" says what the file adds: the body, the braid, the tendon or the cables). The pins are filled in by the render script's --pin, never by hand, and the script refuses a file whose sha256 differs. Kind \"schematic\" is a plain diagram of the type of actuator, drawn by the same script from the description in \"basis\"; it is not the geometry of the published device, and no figure from a paper is copied. Pictures are not to a common scale. Nothing here comes from, or goes into, data/records. An actuator with no entry here keeps the plain round marker.",
